# Title: File Download From Browser Process Via Inline URL
# ID: 94771a71-ba41-4b6e-a757-b531372eaab6
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-01-11
# Tags: attack.command-and-control, attack.t1105
# Description: Detects execution of a browser process with a URL argument pointing to a file with a potentially interesting extension. This can be abused to download arbitrary files or to hide from the user for example by launching the browser in a minimized state.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((((process.command_line:*.7z OR process.command_line:*.dat OR process.command_line:*.dll OR process.command_line:*.exe OR process.command_line:*.hta OR process.command_line:*.ps1 OR process.command_line:*.psm1 OR process.command_line:*.txt OR process.command_line:*.vbe OR process.command_line:*.vbs OR process.command_line:*.zip)) OR ((process.command_line:*.7z\"* OR process.command_line:*.dat\"* OR process.command_line:*.dll\"* OR process.command_line:*.hta\"* OR process.command_line:*.ps1\"* OR process.command_line:*.psm1\"* OR process.command_line:*.txt\"* OR process.command_line:*.vbe\"* OR process.command_line:*.vbs\"* OR process.command_line:*.zip\"*))) AND (process.command_line:*http*) AND ((process.executable:*\\brave.exe OR process.executable:*\\chrome.exe OR process.executable:*\\msedge.exe OR process.executable:*\\opera.exe OR process.executable:*\\vivaldi.exe)))
